"""agy-rpc: an agy agent's session, and an agy account's t3code server, from roster and coordd (the owner, N-1104
p880: "i want to act as t3cdoe so have a t3code -agy logingin basiclly"; p886: "we should just for resrch od ou won
impletion over agy. so like t3code does it but cut out t3 code . just so i can hedge my betse too"; plans N-1446
p2038, read Right in p2039 and p2043).

Two ways to agy (Google's Antigravity CLI), one bridge to coordd:
- **its own ACP client**: `agy acp` of the pinned agy 1.5.18 run by this program, telling agy no client name at all
  (clientInfo is optional in ACP), on a key account's API key (AGY_KEY_FILE) or on a sign-in account's Google sign-in
  (AGY_SIGNIN, the account's profile folder, where agy's own `agy acp --login` keeps it: `signin`).
- **through t3code**, on a sign-in account t3code signed in before agy's own sign-in was used here (T3_HOME, its
  `home/`): the pinned t3code 0.1.11, unmodified, as it ships, one `t3 serve` per account (`server`). An agent is a
  thread of its account's server, driven over t3code's own `/ws`, the interface its web client uses. Nothing of ours
  goes to Google: no client name, no patched code, no flag t3code does not ship with; agy is told t3code's own name by
  t3code. Signing such an account in again (`signin`) moves it to agy's own client.

  agy-rpc serve NAME DIR MODEL[:LEVEL] [SESSION] [--dangerously-skip-permissions]
                                       the agent's session, the way its account gives, exactly one of AGY_KEY_FILE (a
                                       key account's key file) and AGY_SIGNIN (a sign-in account's profile) through
                                       ACP, or T3_HOME (an account t3code signed in) through t3code. roster runs this
                                       under `coordc run NAME --`, so it is the agent's process for coordd. Prints
                                       nothing; SESSION resumes that session (ACP) or thread (t3code), none makes a new
                                       one; its id is written to $CODEX_SOCK/session. AGY_BARE `1` or `true` starts it
                                       bare (`0`, `false` or none: not; any other word is refused). The flag last
                                       starts it in the owner's Yolo (`YOLO`)
  agy-rpc send SESSION PRIORITY TEXT   deliver TEXT, at thinking level $CODEX_EFFORT when set (coord effort). `next` goes into a running turn (t3code's `steer_active`; agy
                                       1.5 steers its running turn with the next ACP prompt) or starts one; `later`
                                       only starts one when no turn runs (exit 3 if one does: the caller keeps it held)
  agy-rpc status SESSION               idle, or busy
  agy-rpc interrupt SESSION            cut the running turn off (coord esc): t3code's `run.interrupt`, ACP's
                                       `session/cancel`; nothing when idle
  agy-rpc wait-idle SESSION            return once no turn runs
  agy-rpc screen                       the agent's terminal (roster's `open`): an imported chat's history (agy-import),
                                       then its transcript as text, followed
  agy-rpc models                       the models agy itself offers, one a line, HOME the account's `home/`: on its key
                                       (AGY_KEY_FILE; its profile HOME/profile) or on its sign-in (AGY_SIGNIN, its
                                       profile); no prompt
  agy-rpc server HOME                  a sign-in account's t3code server (coordd, `accounts::agy`): t3code's documented
                                       settings written into HOME/.t3/userdata/settings.json, then `t3 serve` on
                                       127.0.0.1 alone, in its place (exec), with HOME its home
  agy-rpc signin HOME                  agy's own Google sign-in of the account whose home is HOME (coordd), into its
                                       profile HOME/profile alone (`agy acp --login`): prints `url URL`, Google's
                                       address as agy gives it, reads the code he pasted as one line, gives it to agy,
                                       then prints `succeeded` or `failed WORDS`
  agy-rpc check HOME                   what t3code says of the account, one JSON line: its runtime, sign-in, models
                                       and limits, read again first by t3code's own Refresh (its health check and
                                       Google's quota summary: read only, no prompt, nothing used)
  agy-rpc logout HOME                  the account's sign-out: agy's own (ACP `logout`) on its profile HOME/profile,
                                       or t3code's own on an account t3code signed in

coordd calls send, status, interrupt and wait-idle as it calls codex-rpc (core.rs `rpc_bin`). $CODEX_SOCK names the
agent's coord folder for agy, `$COORD/agents/NAME/agy/coord/` (mode 700), where `serve` keeps:
  ctl          the unix socket the other commands reach the session by (mode 600)
  dir, model   the folder the session runs in, and its model as agy names it (`gemini-…`)
  session      the session's id: t3code's thread id, or agy's ACP session id
  transcript.jsonl
               the session as a Codex rollout (the lines coordd's follow.rs and transcript.rs read): each turn's
               begin and end, the words, each tool call and its output, each request's usage (`token_count`) as Codex
               writes it, so the account's usage rows are read from it as a Codex session's are
Every turn's begin and end, and each tool call's end, are told to coordd by `claude/hook` (prompt, stop, failed,
post) from inside the agent's cgroup, as opencode-rpc tells them.

**Through t3code.** t3code keeps the sign-in in its own state under the account's `home/.t3`; nothing here reads,
prints or copies it. Its server is started with t3code's documented switches and no others: telemetry off by its
environment (`T3CODE_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false`, `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true`, docs/user/telemetry.md), update checks
off, threads Supervised (`approval-required`: t3code asks for each command and file change), its keep-awake, agent
browser and preview tunnel off, and on 127.0.0.1 only: a host that is not loopback is refused before anything starts.
A session's bearer token comes from t3code's own `t3 auth session issue` and stays in this process's memory. Each
approval t3code asks is answered from `claude/hook pre` (allow once, or decline); each question is declined (nobody
is at its form: the model asks through coord). Started by Docket v2's session driver (DOCKET_HOOK_RELAY set), each
moment goes to the relay instead: a call is refused at `tool_called` ({"decline": why}), and the question is then
answered at `permission_asked` ({"answer": "once" | "decline"}); an answer it cannot have or read refuses or
declines. Read-only actions t3code approves itself in Supervised
(docs/user/permission-modes.md: "Some read-only actions can proceed in Supervised"): they reach coordd only as the
tool calls of the transcript. The agent's commands run in its account's server, with the server's environment and
cgroup, so its coord is a program of its own: `$COORD/agents/NAME/agy/bin/coord` (`coord_command`), written at each
start, which runs agent-base's coord with the agent's AGENT_NAME, COORD, COORDD_SOCK and AGENT_BASE, and is named in
the thread's first message. coordc declares the name beside each request, and coordd takes it from the server's
cgroup alone (paper-research N-1446 p2099). t3code 0.1.11 has no system prompt of ours for agy: its only append to
agy's is its own pull-request instructions. So the standing text and that line lead the thread's first message,
after t3code's own instructions. A turn that ends on Google's limit is continued only by the next
message coordd sends after it, as t3code's own Continue (`manualContinuationOfRunId`), never by t3code's
auto-resume or a retry of ours.

**Its own ACP client.** agy is given nothing of its starter's environment but the names PASSED lists (the agent's
own coord names its `coord` needs, none of which a bare agent has, PATH, the locale), and no value naming the owner's
home but inside the coord, agent-base or the agent's own: its own HOME, TMPDIR and XDG folders, no session bus (agy keeps
nothing in a keyring and reaches no one's), no display, no browser, and Google's documented switch that keeps the
pinned binary from updating itself. agy runs with `--disable-telemetry` on a profile folder (`--gemini-dir`, its data
folder APP in it, `--app-data-dir`; agy 1.5.18's `agy acp --help` documents all three):
- on a key, the agent's own (its folder's `home/profile`): the key file, a file of this user's of mode 600, is read
  here and given to agy as `GEMINI_API_KEY` alone, the profile says `"auth": {"type": "gemini-api-key"}` and
  `"modelProvider": "gemini"`, and the session is opened only after agy answered `authenticate` with `gemini-api-key`;
- on a sign-in, the account's (AGY_SIGNIN): agy keeps the sign-in in its data folder there, so each of the account's
  agents runs on that profile with a HOME of its own, after agy answered `authenticate` with `oauth-personal`.
A key is never tried for a sign-in, nor a sign-in for a key: exactly one is given, or nothing starts. Each serve holds
its agent's lock (`serve.lock` in its folder) for as long as it or its agy lives, so no agent is served twice; a
profile's lock (`lock_of`, beside it) is held whole by a key's agent and by a sign-in or sign-out, and shared by a
sign-in's agents and checks, so agy is never signed in or out under a running agent; a profile a sign-in began is no
sign-in until agy took the code (`unfinished`). Left out, on purpose: any client name,
telemetry, the `SSH_CONNECTION` and `AGY_ACP_FORCE_FILE_STORAGE` that t3code sets to steer where agy keeps a sign-in,
anything of the owner's own `~/.gemini` but a chat he imports (agy-import), any read of agy's token or quota, and any
automatic retry of a prompt. Every tool call is asked of coordd first (`"toolPermission": "strict"`, in the profile's
settings.json, mode 600), answered as for t3code; a bare agent, and one in the owner's Yolo, runs with
`--dangerously-skip-permissions` instead, and asks nothing.
"""
import atexit, base64, contextlib, datetime, fcntl, hashlib, ipaddress, json, math, os, pwd, queue, re, shlex, signal, socket, shutil, stat, struct, subprocess, sys, threading, time, traceback, urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request, uuid
from pathlib import Path

C = os.environ.get('CODEX_SOCK', '')

# The one agy the ACP way runs: Antigravity CLI 1.5.18 as agy-pin fetches it into $COORD/opt/agy/1.5.18 (Google's own
# release for linux x64, its archive checked against the sha512 its updater's manifest gives), checked against this
# hash before every run. There is no switch around it: the tests run a copy of this file with their stand-in's hash.
AGY_SHA256 = '7c96ad8c944c1a8d195ca34d2041a3d74d5166c96662b52183b748a3c455d52f'
AGY_VERSION = '1.5.18'
# agy's thinking levels (coord-types' harness.rs, `agy`); agy-import reads these two from here
AGY_LEVELS = ('low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max')

# The one t3code: v0.1.11's linux x64 release as agy-pin fetches it into $COORD/opt/t3/0.1.11 (its archive checked
# against the release's SHA256SUMS), its `t3` checked against this hash before every run. Never `t3 update`.
T3_SHA256 = 'f13dd1f37eb2f719b41f45219b3800412799c80f724b022839b8a133e21aced1'
T3_VERSION = '0.1.11'

# The address a t3code server listens on: loopback only, behind its bearer token (N-1446 p2039). `server` refuses any
# host that is not loopback, and every client here refuses a server that says it listens on one.
T3_HOST = '127.0.0.1'

# t3code's built-in instance of agy, the one these accounts use, and every other built-in instance, each turned off
# in the account's settings so t3code looks for no other harness.
INSTANCE = 'antigravity'
OTHER_INSTANCES = ('codex', 'claudeAgent', 'cursor', 'grok', 'opencode', 'fx', 'kiro', 'muse', 'pi')

# The bearer token's scopes: the thread's reads and acts, and the provider's check and sign-out.
SCOPES = ('orchestration:read', 'orchestration:operate', 'providers:manage')

# A custom agy for the t3code instance (t3code's "Binary path"): None, so t3code runs the runtime it manages and tells
# agy its own name. Only the tests' copy of this file sets it, to their stand-in (N-1446 p2043: "The stand-in stays a
# test-only Binary path").
BINARY_PATH = None

# The t3code methods this program calls, and no other: t3code's reset credits (`provider.consumeResetCredit`) and
# anything that changes its settings are never called (the owner: never his resets or limits).
T3_METHODS = {
    'server.getConfig', 'server.refreshProviders', 'provider.auth.logout', 'orchestration.subscribeShell', 'orchestration.subscribeThread', 'orchestration.launchThread',
    'orchestration.dispatchCommand', 'orchestration.getTurnItem', 'projects.mutate',
}

TERMINAL = ('completed', 'failed', 'interrupted', 'cancelled', 'rolled_back')


# the rest of the program: its parts beside this file's real path, read into its own names in this order
for _part in ('coordd', 't3', 't3_thread', 't3_account', 'acp', 'acp_session'):
    _path = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / f'agy_rpc_{_part}.py'
    exec(compile(_path.read_text(), _path, 'exec'))
del _part, _path


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The session's socket and the commands


def control(session):
    """The session's socket (`ctl`): one JSON line in, one out, from the other commands of this program."""
    path = os.path.join(C, 'ctl')
    try:
        os.unlink(path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass
    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    old = os.umask(0o177)
    try:
        s.bind(path)
    finally:
        os.umask(old)
    s.listen(16)

    def serve_one(conn):
        with conn:
            f = conn.makefile('rw')
            try:
                req = json.loads(f.readline() or '{}')
            except ValueError:
                return
            op, out = req.get('op'), {'ok': True}
            if req.get('session') != session.sid:
                out = {'ok': False, 'why': f'the session here is {session.sid}, not {req.get("session")}'}
            elif op == 'send':
                out['exit'] = session.deliver(str(req.get('text', '')), req.get('prio', 'next'), str(req.get('effort') or ''))
            elif op == 'status':
                out['busy'] = session.busy()
            elif op == 'interrupt':
                session.interrupt()
            elif op == 'wait-idle':
                session.wait_idle()
            else:
                out = {'ok': False, 'why': f'no command {op}'}
            f.write(json.dumps(out) + '\n')
            f.flush()

    def loop():
        while True:
            conn, _ = s.accept()
            threading.Thread(target=serve_one, args=(conn,), daemon=True).start()

    threading.Thread(target=loop, daemon=True).start()


def ask(op, session, **more):
    """One command of the session's socket, its answer."""
    s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    try:
        s.connect(os.path.join(C, 'ctl'))
    except OSError as e:
        sys.exit(f'agy-rpc: no session is served in {C or "$CODEX_SOCK (unset)"} ({e.strerror})')
    with s:
        f = s.makefile('rw')
        f.write(json.dumps(dict(op=op, session=session, **more)) + '\n')
        f.flush()
        out = json.loads(f.readline() or '{}')
    if not out.get('ok'):
        sys.exit(f'agy-rpc: {out.get("why", "no answer")}')
    return out


def imported():
    """The Antigravity CLI chat this agent was imported from (agy-import's `imported`): its conversation, transcript, bytes.
    None where no agent's folder is named (CODEX_SOCK unset: an account's check)."""
    if not C:
        return None
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(C), 'imported')) as f:
            return json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None


def earlier(chat):
    """The imported chat's history as text, read in place from agy's own transcript up to the import's byte."""
    with open(chat['transcript'], 'rb') as f:
        data = f.read(chat['upto'])
    for line in data.splitlines():
        try:
            v = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        text = str(v.get('content') or '').replace('<USER_REQUEST>', '').replace('</USER_REQUEST>', '').strip()
        if v.get('type') == 'USER_INPUT':
            print(f'\nyou: {text}', flush=True)
        elif v.get('type') == 'PLANNER_RESPONSE':
            if text:
                print(f'\nagy: {text}', flush=True)
            for c in v.get('tool_calls') or []:
                print(f'  · {c.get("name")} {json.dumps(c.get("args", {}))[:200]}', flush=True)
        elif v.get('type') == 'CHECKPOINT':
            print('  (compacted)', flush=True)
    print(f'\n  (imported from Antigravity CLI, conversation {chat["conversation"]})', flush=True)


def screen():
    """The agent's terminal: an imported chat's history, then its transcript as text, followed as it grows (roster's `open`)."""
    chat = imported()
    if chat:
        earlier(chat)
    path = os.path.join(C, 'transcript.jsonl')
    while not os.path.exists(path):
        time.sleep(0.5)
    with open(path) as f:
        while True:
            line = f.readline()
            if not line:
                time.sleep(0.3)
                continue
            try:
                v = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            p = v.get('payload') or {}
            kind = p.get('type')
            if kind == 'message':
                text = ''.join(c.get('text', '') for c in p.get('content') or [])
                print(f'\n{"you" if p.get("role") == "user" else "agy"}: {text}', flush=True)
            elif kind == 'function_call':
                print(f'  · {p.get("name")} {p.get("arguments", "")[:200]}', flush=True)
            elif kind in ('task_complete', 'turn_aborted'):
                print(f'  ({"interrupted" if kind == "turn_aborted" else "done"})', flush=True)


# The thinking level in force (roster's MODEL:EFFORT, then coord effort): agy's `thought_level`, one of AGY_LEVELS
EFFORT = ''

# A bare agent (roster's AGY_BARE, `flag`): nothing of ours on it. No standing text and no coord line before its first
# words, no MCP servers, no tool call asked of coordd first: on agy's own client agy runs with
# `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, and through t3code its thread runs in `full-access`; neither asks an approval. Its
# turns' begins and ends, words and usage are still told to coordd, so his words reach it and its answers come back.
BARE = flag('AGY_BARE')

# The owner's Yolo (coordd's `mode`; roster gives it from session.json's `mode`): `serve`'s last argument,
# `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, so that coordd reads it on the command line it starts (coordd's `started_yolo`), as
# it reads Claude Code's. agy runs with that flag and asks nothing, so coordd's check before a call does not run (each
# call is still told after it ran); through t3code its thread runs in `full-access`. Unlike a bare agent it keeps the
# standing text, its MCP servers and every moment told. The profile's settings stay `strict`: a sign-in's profile is
# every agent's on it, and one in Safe asks there.
YOLO = False


def selection(model):
    """t3code's modelSelection for MODEL, with the thinking level when one is asked."""
    return {'instanceId': INSTANCE, 'model': model, **({'options': [{'id': 'thought_level', 'value': EFFORT}]} if EFFORT else {})}


def native_marker():
    """The file whose presence keeps the agent on agy's own client (roster's ROSTER_AGY_NATIVE)."""
    return os.path.join(os.path.dirname(C), 'native')


def serve(name, directory, model, sid):
    model, _, level = model.partition(':')
    if not model or ':' in level:
        sys.exit(f'{name}: {model}:{level} is not MODEL or MODEL:LEVEL; not started')
    os.makedirs(C, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    os.chmod(C, 0o700)
    # the agent's lock, held for as long as this process (and, on agy's own client, its agy) lives: no agent is served
    # twice, and nothing of a running serve's is touched by a second
    mine = hold(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(C), 'serve.lock'))
    if mine is None:
        sys.exit(f'{name}: another agy-rpc serves it ({os.path.dirname(C)}/serve.lock is held); not started')
    write('dir', directory)
    write('model', model)
    for stale in ('session', 'ctl'):
        try:
            os.unlink(os.path.join(C, stale))
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
    home = os.environ.get('T3_HOME', '')
    if home and not (os.environ.get('AGY_KEY_FILE') or os.environ.get('AGY_SIGNIN')):
        if imported() or os.path.exists(native_marker()):
            why = 'it runs on agy\'s own client, and its account was signed in through t3code: sign the account in again first'
            hook('failed', {'error': 'authentication_failed', 'error_details': why})
            sys.exit(f'{name}: {why}; not started')
        serve_t3(name, directory, model, level, sid, os.path.abspath(home))
        return
    way, why = way_of()
    if way is None:
        hook('failed', {'error': 'authentication_failed', 'error_details': why})
        sys.exit(f'{name}: {why}; not started')
    serve_acp(name, directory, model, level, sid, way, mine)


def main(argv):
    global YOLO
    if len(argv) < 2:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    cmd = argv[1]
    if cmd == 'serve':
        args = argv[2:]
        YOLO = args[-1:] == ['--dangerously-skip-permissions']
        args = args[:-1] if YOLO else args
        if not 3 <= len(args) <= 4 or any(a.startswith('--') for a in args):
            sys.exit('usage: agy-rpc serve NAME DIR MODEL [SESSION] [--dangerously-skip-permissions]')
        serve(args[0], args[1], args[2], args[3] if len(args) > 3 else '')
    elif cmd == 'models':
        models()
    elif cmd == 'screen':
        screen()
    elif cmd in ('server', 'signin', 'check', 'logout'):
        if len(argv) < 3:
            sys.exit(f'usage: agy-rpc {cmd} HOME')
        {'server': server, 'signin': signin, 'check': check, 'logout': logout}[cmd](os.path.abspath(argv[2]))
    elif len(argv) < 3:
        sys.exit(__doc__)
    elif cmd == 'send':
        if len(argv) < 5:
            sys.exit('usage: agy-rpc send SESSION PRIORITY TEXT')
        sys.exit(ask('send', argv[2], prio=argv[3], text=argv[4], effort=os.environ.get('CODEX_EFFORT', '')).get('exit', 0))
    elif cmd == 'status':
        print('busy' if ask('status', argv[2]).get('busy') else 'idle')
    elif cmd in ('interrupt', 'wait-idle'):
        ask(cmd, argv[2])
    else:
        sys.exit(__doc__)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main(sys.argv)
